{
  "description": "Corner smoothing (CONTRACT §18.2): Figma's smoothing as in the MIT figma-squircle algorithm with preserveSmoothing false, one radius for all four corners. Inputs: width, height, radius and smoothing (clamped to 0..1). expect gives the effective radius and smoothing, the corner parameters and, for the top-right corner in screen coordinates (y down, angles in degrees from +x, clockwise), the start point, the first cubic (control 1, control 2, end), the arc (centre, radius, start and end angle) and the second cubic. The other corners are the same shape mirrored. Compare with a tolerance of 0.001.",
  "algorithm": [
    "budget = min(width, height) / 2; R = min(radius, budget); if R == 0 the corner is square",
    "s = clamp(smoothing, 0, 1); p = (1 + s) * R; s = min(s, budget / R - 1); p = min(p, budget)",
    "arcMeasure = 90 * (1 - s); arcSectionLength = sin(arcMeasure / 2) * R * sqrt(2)",
    "alpha = (90 - arcMeasure) / 2; p3ToP4 = R * tan(alpha / 2); beta = 45 * s",
    "c = p3ToP4 * cos(beta); d = c * tan(beta); b = (p - arcSectionLength - c - d) / 3; a = 2 * b",
    "top-right corner from (width - p, 0): cubic by (a, 0) (a + b, 0) (a + b + c, d); arc of radius R by (arcSectionLength, arcSectionLength); cubic by (d, c) (d, b + c) (d, a + b + c), ending at (width, p)"
  ],
